רו לו: שלום!","en":"Thus you shall say to him: Peace!","alt":[],"t":"l"},{"he":"הילד רץ הביתה כי ירד גשם.","en":"The child ran home because it rained.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"קדוש היום הזה לה' אלוהינו.","en":"This day is holy to the Lord our God.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"הנה אנוכי עושה דבר חדש.","en":"Behold, I am doing a new thing.","alt":[],"t":"l"}],"hints":{"הנה":"behold / look","הוא":"he / it","בא":"coming / comes","אנוכי":"I (archaic)","שומר":"watches / guards","עליך":"over you / on you","כה":"thus / so","אמר":"said","המלך":"the king","הם":"they","עלו":"went up / ascended","ירושלימה":"toward Jerusalem","ברוך":"blessed","הבא":"the one who comes / welcome","קדוש":"holy / sacred","ימים":"days","באים":"coming (pl.)","לא":"not","ידעתי":"I knew","ה'":"the Lord / God","חזרו":"returned (pl.)","הביתה":"homeward / home","שמו":"his name","לעולם":"forever","המקום":"the place","הזה":"this (m.)","באה":"comes (f.) / has come","השעה":"the hour","הולך":"goes / walks","לפניך":"before you","ייעשה":"shall be done","לכל":"to every / to all","אדם":"person / man","הילדים":"the children","הלכו":"went / walked (pl.)","אתה":"you (m.)","אלוהינו":"our God","יום":"day","שולח":"sending","מלאך":"messenger / angel","דיבר":"spoke","הנביא":"the prophet","אל":"to / toward","העם":"the people","היא":"she","נסעה":"traveled (f.)","הגבר":"the man","אשר":"who / which / that","יבטח":"trusts / will trust","האור":"the light","מן":"from","המזרח":"the east","עמך":"with you","בכל":"in every / in all","מקום":"place","שמרו":"keep! (pl.) / guard!","משפט":"justice / judgment","אחרי":"after","החג":"the holiday","וברוך":"and blessed","כי":"because / that / for","טוב":"good","אלוהיך":"your God","לי":"to me","אבי":"my father","עלה":"went up","לרגל":"for a pilgrimage","ברוכה":"blessed (f.)","הבאה":"the one who comes (f.)","למשפחה":"to the family","לכולם":"to everyone","נתתי":"I gave / I have given","לך":"to you","את":"(object marker)","הארץ":"the land / the earth","תאמרו":"you shall say (pl.)","לו":"to him","שלום":"peace / hello","הילד":"the child","רץ":"ran / running","ירד":"fell / rained","גשם":"rain","היום":"the day / today","עושה":"doing / makes","דבר":"thing","חדש":"new","לה":"to her","ה":"God / the Lord"},"words":[{"he":"הנה","en":"behold","alt":["look"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"hineh"},{"he":"אנוכי","en":"I (archaic)","alt":[],"from":"lexicon","tr":"anokhi"},{"he":"כה אמר","en":"thus said","alt":[],"from":"lexicon","tr":"ko amar"},{"he":"ירושלימה","en":"toward Jerusalem","alt":[],"from":"lexicon","tr":"yerushalaimah"},{"he":"הביתה","en":"homeward","alt":["home"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"habaitah"},{"he":"ברוך","en":"blessed","alt":[],"from":"lexicon","tr":"barukh"},{"he":"קדוש","en":"holy","alt":["sacred"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"kadosh"},{"he":"מלאך","en":"messenger","alt":["angel"],"from":"skill","tr":"mal'akh"},{"he":"נביא","en":"prophet","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"navi"},{"he":"אשר","en":"who / which","alt":["that"],"from":"skill","tr":"asher"},{"he":"משפט","en":"justice","alt":["judgment"],"from":"skill","tr":"mishpat"},{"he":"ברוכה","en":"blessed (f.)","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"brukhah"},{"he":"קדושה","en":"holy (f.)","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"kdoshah"},{"he":"אלוהינו","en":"our God","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"eloheinu"},{"he":"אלוהיך","en":"your God","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"elohekha"},{"he":"לרגל","en":"for a pilgrimage","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"laregel"},{"he":"כה","en":"thus","alt":["so"],"from":"phrase","tr":"ko"},{"he":"שמרו","en":"keep! (pl.)","alt":["guard!"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"עמך","en":"with you","alt":[],"from":"phrase","tr":"imkha"}],"lexemes":["הנה","אנוכי","כה","ירושלימה","הביתה","ברוך","ברוכה","קדוש","קדושה","מלאך","נביא","אשר","משפט","אלוהינו","אלוהיך","לרגל","שמרו","עמך"],"tips":"## More Biblical Hebrew Patterns\n\n### The Directional ה (הא המגמה)\nIn biblical Hebrew, a ה suffix indicates direction or motion toward:\n- **ירושלימה** -- toward Jerusalem\n- **הביתה** -- homeward\n- **מצרימה** -- toward Egypt\n- **ארצה** -- toward the ground\n\nThis survives in modern Hebrew: הביתה (going home) is used daily.\n\n### Archaic Pronoun: אנוכי\n**אנוכי** is the archaic form of **אני** (I). It appears in the Ten Commandments: אָנֹכִי ה' אֱלֹהֶיךָ -- I am the Lord your God.\n\n### Prophetic Formula: כה אמר\n**כה אמר ה'** (Thus said the Lord) introduces divine speech throughout the prophetic books. כה means \"thus\" or \"so.\"\n\n### Common Blessings\n- **ברוך** (blessed) opens most Jewish blessings: ברוך אתה ה' אלוהינו\n- **קדוש** (holy) describes God, the Sabbath, and sacred spaces\n- **ברוך הבא** (welcome, lit. \"blessed is he who comes\") is used daily in modern Hebrew\n\n### The Infinitive Absolute: הלוך\nThe infinitive absolute emphasizes action:\n- הָלוֹךְ הָלַךְ = he walked and walked (emphatic)"}